WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.135
How do we turn what we learn
about people

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.800
into a product that works?

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.820
Each step requires a different
kind of judgment.

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.360
We start with three synthetic
interviews.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.060
Researchers describe lost context,

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:14.530
inconsistent codes,

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.360
and findings that others
cannot easily verify.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.560
We code the episodes.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.900
Ward clustering groups episodes
two and three first.

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.600
This reveals similarity,
not requirements.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.400
Clustering is optional.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.600
We return to the evidence.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.480
One researcher wants every claim
linked to its source.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.740
That helps us propose
a requirement for the design.

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.855
The Fit Check compares
three designs

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.640
against the same requirements.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:43.590
Two meet the essentials.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.175
We choose the evidence workspace

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.440
for better reuse,
despite its higher cost.

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:51.900
Reverse Fit asks why
each part belongs.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.980
We defer a weekly digest.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.820
It may be useful, but it exceeds
this release's budget.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:02.020
The breadboard shows how
the selected design works.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:03.860
A researcher codes an excerpt,

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:05.310
the comparison updates,

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.340
and a finding links
to its evidence.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.500
Unsupported findings are blocked.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.660
Finally, we test
three things separately.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.415
Does the link work?

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.280
Does the evidence support
the claim?

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.940
And does the product
actually improve the work?

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.440
The goal is to keep
the reasoning visible:

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.020
what we observed,
what we inferred,

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:27.855
what we chose, how it works,

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:30.300
and what reality tells us
to change.
